From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LvglLib: Leave the UEFI header bindings out of lvgl.h

LVGL v9.6 moved its public headers into include/lvgl, and lvgl.h now
includes all of them, with the two header bindings of the UEFI driver:
lv_uefi_edk2.h, which includes EDK2's Uefi.h and protocols, and
lv_uefi_gnu_efi.h, which includes gnu-efi's efi.h. A build has one of
the two frameworks, not both, so with LV_USE_UEFI every file that
includes lvgl.h stops on the other one. With EDK2:

  lvgl/include/lvgl/drivers/uefi/lv_uefi_gnu_efi.h:13:14: fatal error:
  efi.h: No such file or directory

The binding is the one that LV_USE_UEFI_INCLUDE names ("lv_uefi_edk2.h"
in lv_conf.h), and lv_uefi.h includes it already. Leave the two out of
lvgl.h, which up to v9.5 had no UEFI header at all. The master branch
of LVGL has the same two lines.

TEST=LvglPkg.dsc builds with LVGL v9.6 (release/v9.6 at bb1ff0af416c).
---
 Library/LvglLib/lvgl/include/lvgl/lvgl.h | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Library/LvglLib/lvgl/include/lvgl/lvgl.h b/Library/LvglLib/lvgl/include/lvgl/lvgl.h
index 7c7e8a6..e674e3f 100644
--- a/Library/LvglLib/lvgl/include/lvgl/lvgl.h
+++ b/Library/LvglLib/lvgl/include/lvgl/lvgl.h
@@ -107,8 +107,6 @@
 #include "drivers/uefi/lv_uefi.h"
 #include "drivers/uefi/lv_uefi_context.h"
 #include "drivers/uefi/lv_uefi_display.h"
-#include "drivers/uefi/lv_uefi_edk2.h"
-#include "drivers/uefi/lv_uefi_gnu_efi.h"
 #include "drivers/uefi/lv_uefi_indev.h"
 #include "drivers/wayland/lv_wayland.h"
 #include "drivers/wayland/lv_wayland_keyboard.h"
-- 
